  "notes": "INTERNET SLANG:\nA verb derived from the search engine \"Google,\" meaning to search for something online. This is a common example of brand-name verbification in Japanese.\n\nConjugates as a godan verb: ググる → ググった → ググ⟦って→って：29146_tte⟧ → ググれば\n\nWRITING:\nTypically written in katakana (ググる) rather than hiragana.\n\nREGISTER: Casual/informal. Common in everyday speech among younger generations.\n\nNOTE: While \"ググる\" specifically implies using Google, it's often used generically for any internet search, similar to how \"to google\" is used in English.",
